  "summary": "Bloomington, Indiana announced it did not renew its Flock LPR contract, which expired March 5, 2026, after a months-long evaluation. During the transition, Mayor Thomson restricted Flock data access to BPD personnel only and ended outside data sharing, while the City evaluates alternative technologies.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Mayor Kerry Thomson announced today that the City's contract for Flock LPR services expired on March 5, 2026, and that, following a months-long evaluation, the City decided not to renew it.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Access to Flock data will be limited to Bloomington Police Department personnel only. There will be no outside data sharing.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "This review made clear that if this tool is used, it must be used under narrow parameters, strong accountability, and clear public safeguards.",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    }
